  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Study on pathways to Nigeria potato seeds market</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this study is to identify credible pathways to market for the international (Dutch) private sector to offer access to quality potato planting material to smallholder farmers in Nigeria, specifically in Plateau State. This will be done by identifying alternative business models (best-bet pathways) based on experiences in Nigeria itself and relevant cases from other African countries with comparable difficult enabling environment for investments and market access. The overall goal is to contribute to food security and nutrition, promote Dutch and Nigerian investments and stimulate job creation and entrepreneurship. This is in line and contributes to the strategy of the Embassy of the Netherlands in Abuja including combination track horticulture &amp; starting materials to keep the agriculture sector growing.</narrative>
  </description>
